  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively be the eccentricity and length of the latus rectum of the hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively the eccentricity and length of the latus rectum of its conjugate hyperbola. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>77</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>44</mn><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
